   "area_id": "ca_four_gables_peak_12_801_peak_12_808",
   "name": "Direct East Face",
   "grade": "5.10+",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Ten pitches directly up the middle of Four Gables South (Peak 12,801'), on the east side. Rock is grainy and loose. Pitches 1-4 are easy and simul-climbed, about 500'. Sandy ledges and cracks form the 200' fifth (5.10-). Hardest is the 150' sixth pitch, 5.10+: corner crack, then a roof that is strenuous. The seventh, 5.10 and 100', passes stacked blocks that are serious: push softly, never pull, since the belayer stands directly below. Pitches 8-9, about 250' at 5.6, reach a cave; a tunnel then leads out for the 5.7 final pitch of 100'.",
