   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Ten pitches of mostly moderate climbing with some steeper crack cruxes, on generally good rock. Pitch 1 is an approach pitch (5.6, 30m) up a dike. Pitches 2-4 run 5.7 to 5.8 up flakes, corners and a V groove to the crest. Pitches 5 and 6 (both 5.9+) are steep cracks. Pitches 7 and 8 get past a small tower on loose ground. Pitch 9 (5.8) is a corner by the prow; pitch 10 (5.7) traverses left to the top.",
